#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133513 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f260476d-35d0-504a-9e0a-86f7fb0049bd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/id #uuid "1ad2672a-5773-5f2e-ab81-64e51ab4a7e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5570" :question/problem "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/8a460dfb89b0d2e9c1e197aa212f494971df1c36822117fb4b1271f5608d1d1a.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/a172f54b0dc879c2363cfd2818fc79614d68662def6dd56b0ac9aec8fdbca1a5.png) Find the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{b}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{b}\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 9+0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-1)}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4+9+0-1}{4+1+0+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133514 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/id #uuid "2031cdd7-c43e-509c-8bb2-4d7362914e7b" :question/math-academy-id "e-5571" :question/problem "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/fb060fbc7ac20ff3b739a7c8958b4977e72abd31679c098973395db99fb6f78e.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/7a20f39cb1c7c36a01e9d7d4dcd8cbe619c8cffacb57bc2bf42b8d46ce53bb5b.png) If $\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{y} + \\mathbf{z},$ where $\\mathbf{y} \\in \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ and $\\mathbf{z} \\perp \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\},$ then find $\\mathbf{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "A diagram of the situation is provided below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-4)+0\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4+0-2}{1+1+0+1}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}a \\\\  & =2a \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\mathbf{y} \\in \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ and $\\mathbf{z} \\perp \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\},$ as shown in the picture above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133515 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto the Solution Space of a System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "5168f07e-4a22-5e0c-a612-e5c6f77f99eb" :question/math-academy-id "e-5572" :question/problem "Given the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the solution space of the system.\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/37beee87c5b5bd6350bd2c0f6353b61b1cfd321449a96b8b66aac99584d459bb.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, $x_3$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get $x_2=4x_3.$ \nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain  \n\n$$\nx_1+4x_3+4x_3= 0\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx_1=-8x_3.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/4995b9959cbb8a412fe0ed6198bfa9a82bcda40cd388c4759589e060ec16de1e.png)\nConsequently, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/232c58060c7ba67f66564e8f8667fe67a84f6ef886a1c56e2d042224ace9b4db.png) is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-10)\\cdot (-8)+20\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 1}{{(-8)}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{80+80+2}{64+16+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{162}{81}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f260476d-35d0-504a-9e0a-86f7fb0049bd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c57186e7-acdd-556b-9a79-a59b057071a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353154} {:answer/id #uuid "78e4cfed-2612-57ae-a2d3-d2024101c730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353155} {:answer/id #uuid "d935319d-0576-5f76-9c1a-9e89ba8fcb1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353156} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7f9b0b-5d04-5c5f-9f54-1077e38b86e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353157} {:answer/id #uuid "8f3419b4-7bc0-5c39-bfb7-366c36f29c7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78e4cfed-2612-57ae-a2d3-d2024101c730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353155} :answer-field/id #uuid "6182e784-b047-5409-b54f-fbb1b830013a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f05980d-4426-5706-8a2c-5e2131836b68" :question/math-academy-id "q-140114" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 8+1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 10+2\\cdot 6}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{8+4-10+12}{1+1+1+4}b \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{7}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f260476d-35d0-504a-9e0a-86f7fb0049bd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cd575b9-dced-5687-b011-3cbbecd8a4f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353161} {:answer/id #uuid "334dbaba-e32a-57f7-84c4-5e2229e0f4ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353162} {:answer/id #uuid "967c7043-9b00-5804-8e02-571feffbee1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353163} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9d60a5-f723-53f8-8844-ee3ca2b5acfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353164} {:answer/id #uuid "e59c3df9-b5ef-5e74-aed1-249775cc4dc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "334dbaba-e32a-57f7-84c4-5e2229e0f4ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353162} :answer-field/id #uuid "f171189a-dae4-5699-8486-5a4eabb311b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ad7228fc-9e28-545a-880f-30ac45a1913e" :question/math-academy-id "q-140115" :question/problem "Let $b=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 30 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}.$" :question/worked-solution "The vector projection of $b$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 12+(-1)\\cdot 30+0\\cdot 12+1\\cdot 24}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{12-30+0+24}{1+1+0+1}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}a \\\\  & =2a \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60ba02e7-9700-57e0-b0e8-a1f409d7d096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353168} {:answer/id #uuid "b210a479-f250-5920-9d04-48eb1b721688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353169} {:answer/id #uuid "37a23596-8ad5-5769-a981-db209e2eda1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353170} {:answer/id #uuid "66d840c3-9a32-538e-8441-912f2cecfc8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353171} {:answer/id #uuid "860e3b86-1117-53fc-b6bf-f4784c0a9903" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ba02e7-9700-57e0-b0e8-a1f409d7d096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353168} :answer-field/id #uuid "46ab8976-0de5-5437-b164-2afebcc12886" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d62d6869-fd0d-50a4-9c77-6fb492970304" :question/math-academy-id "q-140117" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot (-5)+6\\cdot 5+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+30+6+4}{4+36+4+16}a \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{60}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto the Solution Space of a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e77f955-361d-5749-89d2-fa7e25e42e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353175} {:answer/id #uuid "7f4841d6-de1d-5c16-a723-4c57b0beb550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353176} {:answer/id #uuid "8d944ace-c8c5-52d7-b560-796af07c4d3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353177} {:answer/id #uuid "bb060b3c-ce48-5925-9266-531aef721cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353178} {:answer/id #uuid "e011a09b-a740-54a1-ba76-6e7fa3a541f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d944ace-c8c5-52d7-b560-796af07c4d3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353177} :answer-field/id #uuid "c719a775-1b0d-5fc7-9055-195354f657a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b76f14de-8a84-5055-bcfe-22640334e836" :question/math-academy-id "q-140119" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}$ and from the second equation ${x}_{2}=-3{x}_{3}.$  \n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{22}{11}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd8ace83-da01-51dc-8b7c-5c6c39cf2c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131391} {:answer/id #uuid "c89cbf41-ee8b-5e84-88fd-7b88b0ee146d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131392} {:answer/id #uuid "ea496413-55f6-513d-8635-c1ccb5f3cc52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131393} {:answer/id #uuid "2011453f-5f42-511b-824e-e7871b71ed24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131394} {:answer/id #uuid "57361eb1-cf6b-5408-9965-10f36a3c6dad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea496413-55f6-513d-8635-c1ccb5f3cc52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131393} :answer-field/id #uuid "58166b90-bd2b-519c-a312-56af3e9fc048" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "093d7617-4a17-5d9a-be95-4758456c60a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-39712" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 12+6\\cdot 6+(-6)\\cdot (-6)+2\\cdot 12}{{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+{2}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{24+36+36+24}{4+36+36+4}a \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{80}a \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}a \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f260476d-35d0-504a-9e0a-86f7fb0049bd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5728ec81-98a3-5a8a-bcae-f5dc3a0ae1e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{21}{10} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{21}{10} \\\\ \\frac{14}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353182} {:answer/id #uuid "67cc083f-3ff8-58e1-8809-c5d67efc74db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353183} {:answer/id #uuid "79c3d564-ad86-5f67-aa68-4aac644dea00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353184} {:answer/id #uuid "84d34fbf-c877-5e3a-9005-53efa199ba51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353185} {:answer/id #uuid "88e9a7e1-325d-5276-9d0c-fd079099c9d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{14}{5} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{21}{10} \\\\ \\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88e9a7e1-325d-5276-9d0c-fd079099c9d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{14}{5} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{21}{10} \\\\ \\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353186} :answer-field/id #uuid "64cb133e-98f9-5eb4-a6ec-8160361d30e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9643dc7c-31e8-5469-acd7-713795ad19d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-39727" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 4}{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4+9+4}{16+4+9+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{30}b \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}b \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{14}{5} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{21}{10} \\\\ \\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ad20cec-f18a-5b07-a179-8b6979ac4d84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353189} {:answer/id #uuid "571d9150-15f4-5dca-9d0d-0c1b1b82063e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353190} {:answer/id #uuid "dc552ee6-6e68-504f-991a-55699c81f4b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353191} {:answer/id #uuid "c338bda0-8400-5332-a7d1-1e2b1d701cde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{9}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353192} {:answer/id #uuid "62edd632-6d64-5ece-944c-93df2076b37c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ad20cec-f18a-5b07-a179-8b6979ac4d84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353189} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe94e0e4-f6d2-5fba-b941-3226323aa6b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8573fb3d-1127-5d21-8467-27317571f1e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-39729" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 6+3\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 6}{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6+9+9+6}{1+9+9+1}a \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{20}a \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}a \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dbf9794-75eb-5d07-b4f2-ad75cb664d30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353196} {:answer/id #uuid "31dcae60-f019-5c84-89a9-c55a32b2d545" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353197} {:answer/id #uuid "8e3131be-0858-543c-b47f-17caea5dbef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353198} {:answer/id #uuid "c12e3144-4335-5e78-8192-dcc149fe9482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353199} {:answer/id #uuid "a1122b54-fb7d-578a-bd25-a493da5b4631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1122b54-fb7d-578a-bd25-a493da5b4631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353200} :answer-field/id #uuid "f366f5df-e72b-516e-b0ce-1eb53e470b8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3862e17b-0289-5fb6-b72e-c3913eaf442a" :question/math-academy-id "q-40409" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find the distance between $x$ and $\\text{Span}{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The distance between the vector $x$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by $‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖$, where $\\overset{^}{x}$ in the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{span}{b}.$\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{b\\cdot x}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-4)+(-3)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 3}{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\text{ }\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{6+0+6+0}{9+0+9+0}\\text{ }\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\text{ }\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+((-4)-0)^{2}+((-2)-(-2))^{2}+(3-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16+0+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto the Solution Space of a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e18bb46-3c6e-5e3a-bb5a-665f306c88b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131721} {:answer/id #uuid "e714e48d-334b-58dd-9d78-ca84470ef688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131722} {:answer/id #uuid "07f16a69-4168-5892-9e11-858f9fd00067" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131723} {:answer/id #uuid "0c194c75-24a2-57c1-a5e2-8181f08fb4d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131724} {:answer/id #uuid "6fa4baf6-d9e9-5150-97e2-7833cb8e2f45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c194c75-24a2-57c1-a5e2-8181f08fb4d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131724} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ff09d50-84a2-5ac6-9658-713916400c9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c185f4ac-1057-5248-8964-7fb26d1dea03" :question/math-academy-id "q-40425" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 1}{{(-1)}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-8}{2}b \\\\  & =-4b \\\\  & =-4[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f260476d-35d0-504a-9e0a-86f7fb0049bd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5a902dd-e29f-5f70-b355-a378a86e6e3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353203} {:answer/id #uuid "4eeeb1a2-5bc3-5150-aa30-f689b76c4e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353204} {:answer/id #uuid "9d29fe9b-31fa-5e0e-b839-2a6d8668834e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353205} {:answer/id #uuid "94551a23-11c0-5108-974d-235fb844e393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353206} {:answer/id #uuid "831f39e9-9ebf-5ac4-a8b8-62175c1523e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4eeeb1a2-5bc3-5150-aa30-f689b76c4e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353204} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f60f5b4-e15c-5c5b-bad6-045c67062b70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f3e3378b-fc8a-5168-a3c5-b0611c57d399" :question/math-academy-id "q-81124" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 5}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2+2+0+5}{1+1+0+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{3}b \\\\  & =3b \\\\  & =3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto the Solution Space of a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60fd872f-404f-5562-99ef-a64931cd8557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353210} {:answer/id #uuid "cb87f663-5ccd-54db-80bf-2809b22507ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353211} {:answer/id #uuid "c8e03b9b-61aa-57c8-9e2f-578844db2c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353212} {:answer/id #uuid "3eed2c63-6931-54c5-92fb-c4f19935d8b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353213} {:answer/id #uuid "11a6c226-cdcc-542a-99b4-23a96264a863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60fd872f-404f-5562-99ef-a64931cd8557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353210} :answer-field/id #uuid "184ce97b-ec25-52e6-a5f4-d63b5ebd5d94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f7628d96-7413-59a8-b813-69718d9f2735" :question/math-academy-id "q-81196" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3}b \\\\  & =4b \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto the Solution Space of a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69c2f9d8-51e9-556e-8204-c724a3d5d84f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353217} {:answer/id #uuid "1d5869a3-9c6c-5144-8b07-a2e8fc425c06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353218} {:answer/id #uuid "03e1163e-b88d-5484-b4a3-68cbf39c712a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353219} {:answer/id #uuid "1f793a48-dfbf-5c20-a8c5-e0dbe63606c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353220} {:answer/id #uuid "3b9c687c-4b48-5748-9143-c39279e56106" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b9c687c-4b48-5748-9143-c39279e56106" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353221} :answer-field/id #uuid "0585e468-45e4-50cc-86a1-46acd21d4bcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bcc8ff8e-bf46-5901-8fed-da7d7df3ad36" :question/math-academy-id "q-81199" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+3\\cdot 1}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\frac{1}{4}+1}b \\\\  & =4b \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto the Solution Space of a System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ee4b450-5be0-53a9-99a0-22e008127944" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353224} {:answer/id #uuid "c437f2dd-4de5-5439-88ad-ceba0f35ea1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353225} {:answer/id #uuid "1c9fefc9-f782-5e47-8f7e-3d17727c9f9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353226} {:answer/id #uuid "938b8c44-0756-587a-98c2-8ca66c22427c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353227} {:answer/id #uuid "918ae809-248d-561f-8236-5fe0c1b51f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "938b8c44-0756-587a-98c2-8ca66c22427c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353227} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3f8d76b-29d9-5db6-b00d-6b11a0911a16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8bc5c35e-337a-5a6f-8888-1b0686935cc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-81200" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3\\cdot (2{x}_{3})=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=6{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 6+5\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 1}{{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{82}{41}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f260476d-35d0-504a-9e0a-86f7fb0049bd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85fd6813-d910-5972-ad6e-bb74323a4836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353231} {:answer/id #uuid "d9a6c95e-0f7b-5d43-9880-1eeb781287f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353232} {:answer/id #uuid "4b70dfc2-9ff9-5963-85a8-7a0bfe0228c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353233} {:answer/id #uuid "63f49621-0914-5e62-9b75-11ed0126edf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353234} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e242d3-fd2b-5641-957d-9ce34004d5ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b70dfc2-9ff9-5963-85a8-7a0bfe0228c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353233} :answer-field/id #uuid "f84d4059-fe92-50d9-bbff-8ffaae6a9730" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2d04d271-7f30-57f2-8fbb-89c0c493d46b" :question/math-academy-id "q-86727" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot 8+(-1)\\cdot (-6)}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4+(-4)+24+6}{4+1+9+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{15}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "144d1258-f8d5-55e9-be38-ec25b6f84bd3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5054405-facf-54f5-bdfe-871b9c04b5f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353238} {:answer/id #uuid "360fe14b-b8cf-5166-ab3d-44b0b412fb7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353239} {:answer/id #uuid "4f5ca75b-30c4-5a20-9400-b0dcb2433959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353240} {:answer/id #uuid "ab2bbbee-db70-5bc9-bb2d-669a368c145a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353241} {:answer/id #uuid "8b436eb3-bea4-568d-a772-0a7f9c13ed6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f5ca75b-30c4-5a20-9400-b0dcb2433959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353240} :answer-field/id #uuid "297cc6f2-9518-5974-8a04-deeb08818110" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "728a5fb3-dd12-5d29-849a-69191460d4d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-86733" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066555/assets/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 4}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{3+2+(-2)+12}{1+4+1+9}a \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{15}a \\\\  & =a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$"}]}
